# Reachability keep-out. Wikis that are DELIBERATELY standalone -- process, harness, or
# methodology documents with no survey host, whose readers arrive from CLAUDE.md, a rule,
# a plan, or a report rather than from a survey section.
#
# `crosslink.py reach` reports every wiki under wikis/ that no survey can reach by a
# reader-facing link (mentions inside HTML comments do NOT count -- they are invisible in
# the rendered page). Anything not listed here must be linked from the section it supports.
#
# This is NOT the same list as .claude/crosslink-keepout. That one declares "not in any
# TF-IDF corpus group"; this one declares "no survey reader is expected to arrive here".
# A doc can legitimately be in one, both, or neither.
